from build import *
from urllib.parse import quote

RULES={
'Ward':{'definition':'Absorb incoming damage before HP. Player Ward expires at the start of the next player turn. Old enemy Ward expires when its next action begins, after Burn, even if Hush skips that action.','notes':['Ward stops damage, not separate status or card-movement effects.','No trait checks whether damage reached Ward or HP.']},
'Burn':{'definition':'At player turn end, deal Flame damage equal to Burn, then reduce it by 1. Resolve player Burn first, then enemy Burn. Applying Burn keeps the higher value; it does not add.','notes':['Ward absorbs Burn. Burn receives no Mark, weakness, Leech or Reflect effect.','An enemy applies Burn after this tick; that Burn first ticks at the following player turn end.']},
'Scry':{'definition':'Look at the top card of your draw pile. You may put it on the bottom. If the draw pile is empty, shuffle the discard pile first; if both are empty, do nothing.','notes':[]},
'Mark':{'definition':'Add Mark to the next direct attack against its holder, before Ward, then remove Mark. Mark adds together and affects only the first hit.','notes':['The player normally Marks the enemy; an enemy effect explicitly names the player when it Marks them.','Mark does not affect Burn or separate trait damage.']},
'Weaken':{'definition':'Reduce the holder’s next direct attack by Weaken, to a minimum of 0, then remove Weaken. Weaken adds together and affects only the first hit.','notes':['Weaken persists through non-attack actions.','A player effect says “Weaken 4”; an enemy effect explicitly applies Weaken to the player.']},
'Hush':{'definition':'Suppress the enemy’s labeled trait through its next action. Skip a non-attack ability; an attack keeps its base hits. Advance the pattern normally.','notes':['Hush starts immediately and ends after the action’s aftereffects, including traits active while the intent is shown.','Hush does not undo existing Ward, damage, revealed cards, or an already-applied next-turn effect.','Hush does not stack. A pure Hush card needs a suppressible ability or trait in the current intent. A conditional trait counts even before its condition is met.','Every current Hush face Banishes its source.']},
'Keep':{'definition':'Keep the chosen card through this turn’s discard. It remains on its current face and loses its Keep marker. Next turn draw up to 5 new cards within the 8-card hand cap.','notes':['The resolving source is outside the hand and cannot be kept. A card leaving the hand loses its marker.','Enemy references to held cards check the actual hand after unkept cards are discarded; no retained-card snapshot or prior identity is stored.']},
'Flip':{'definition':'Turn cards to their other faces. “Flip your hand” affects only cards currently in hand; other zones change only when explicitly named.','notes':['The resolving source never flips with its own hand effect.','Cards keep their faces through movement and reshuffling.']},
'Banish':{'definition':'Remove the physical card, including both faces, for this fight. Return it to the run deck afterward. Banished cards cannot be recovered during a fight.','notes':['This spends the depicted opportunity for the encounter; it need not mean that a depicted creature literally dies.','An enemy’s Banish can remove a player card; show its destination and that it returns after the fight.']},
'Reflect':{'definition':'Redirect the next attack’s first hit to its attacker, keeping its final damage and type. Then Reflect ends. Reflect does not stack.','notes':['Apply Mark, weakness and Weaken before reflection; do not apply them again at the new target. The attacker’s Ward can absorb the returned hit unless the hit ignores Ward.','A reflected hit cannot be reflected again. A 0-damage hit still spends Reflect. Burn and separate trait damage are not attacks.','A trait may specify an earlier expiry, such as the end of its displayed intent. Hush suspends that trait’s reflection immediately.']},
'Leech':{'definition':'Heal for the attack’s final damage after bonuses and Weaken, before Ward. Count Ward absorption and overkill. Healing stops at maximum HP.','notes':['For multiple hits with Leech, total their final damage values; do not track HP actually lost.','Leech is healing attached to that attack, not a damage type or a second hidden effect. It cannot revive an attacker already defeated.','Food, medicine and other fixed heals remain fixed heals.']},
}

CSS='''
:root{color-scheme:dark;--bg:#111218;--panel:#1b1e27;--ink:#eee9df;--muted:#bbb4c3;--line:#42404d;--accent:#e9c58b}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:16px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1280px;margin:auto;padding:44px 28px 68px}header{max-width:960px;margin-bottom:26px}h1{font:normal clamp(34px,5vw,58px)/1.12 Georgia,serif;margin:12px 0 20px}h2{font:normal 29px/1.2 Georgia,serif;margin:0 0 18px}h3{font-size:18px;margin:18px 0 8px}p{margin:0 0 14px}a{color:var(--accent);text-underline-offset:3px}.eyebrow,.number{color:var(--accent);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}.muted,footer{color:var(--muted)}.notice{border-left:3px solid var(--accent);padding:15px 20px;background:#292432}.panel,.pair,.enemy,.audit{padding:24px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;background:var(--panel);margin-bottom:20px}.faces{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:25px}.side{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em}.effect{font-size:18px;line-height:1.6}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:22px;align-items:start}.enemy{padding:0;overflow:hidden;margin:0}.art{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:4/3;object-fit:contain;background:#090a0e}.entry{padding:22px}.entry h2{font-size:27px}.actions{padding-left:20px}.actions li{margin:12px 0}.tools{display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:end;margin:28px 0}.tools label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;font-size:13px}input,select,button{font:inherit;background:#22232d;color:var(--ink);border:1px solid #777081;padding:10px;border-radius:4px}input{width:min(380px,75vw)}button{cursor:pointer}:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:3px}.count{color:var(--muted);padding:10px 0}details{margin:18px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:650;color:var(--accent)}details p{margin-top:12px}dl{margin:0}dt{font-weight:650;margin:14px 0 5px}dd{margin:0 0 12px}.rule{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:12px}.table-wrap{overflow:auto}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}th,td{text-align:left;padding:10px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top}li{margin:7px 0}.small{font-size:14px}.section{margin:48px 0 24px}.toc{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px 18px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding-bottom:20px}.portrait-grid{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap}.portrait-grid img{max-width:200px;height:auto;max-height:240px;object-fit:contain}.audit .changed{color:#f2c084}.audit .before{color:var(--muted)}footer{margin-top:40px;font-size:13px}[hidden]{display:none!important}@media(max-width:1050px){.grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:620px){main{padding:26px 18px}.grid,.faces{grid-template-columns:1fr}.panel,.pair,.audit{padding:18px}.entry{padding:20px}.tools{display:block}.tools label{margin-bottom:12px}}@media print{body{background:white;color:#111;font:10pt/1.4 Arial,sans-serif}main{padding:0}.tools,.toc{display:none}.panel,.pair,.enemy,.audit{background:white;border-color:#bbb;break-inside:avoid}.grid{display:block}.enemy{display:grid;grid-template-columns:27% 1fr;margin-bottom:18px}.art{margin-top:20px}.entry{padding:14px}h2{font-size:18pt}.notice{background:#eee}a,.muted,.side,footer,summary{color:#333}.effect span,dd span,li span{color:#222!important}}
'''

def page(title,body,script=''):
 return '<!doctype html>\n<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>'+html.escape(title)+'</title><style>'+CSS+styles()+'</style></head><body><main>'+body+'</main>'+('<script>'+script+'</script>' if script else '')+'</body></html>\n'
def filter_script(selector,total):
 return f'''const items=[...document.querySelectorAll('{selector}')],input=document.querySelector('#search'),choice=document.querySelector('#choice');function filter(){{const q=input.value.trim().toLocaleLowerCase();let n=0;for(const el of items){{const show=(!q||el.dataset.search.includes(q))&&(!choice||!choice.value||el.dataset.filter.split(' ').includes(choice.value));el.hidden=!show;if(show)n++;}}document.querySelector('#count').textContent=n+' / {total}';}}input.addEventListener('input',filter);if(choice)choice.addEventListener('change',filter);document.querySelector('#reset').addEventListener('click',()=>{{input.value='';if(choice)choice.value='';filter();}});'''
def tools(total,label='Search names and effect text',options=None):
 opts='' if not options else '<label>Filter<select id="choice"><option value="">All entries</option>'+''.join(f'<option value="{html.escape(v)}">{html.escape(t)}</option>' for v,t in options)+'</select></label>'
 return f'<div class="tools" role="search"><label>{label}<input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Search…"></label>{opts}<button type="button" id="reset">Reset</button><span id="count" class="count" aria-live="polite">{total} / {total}</span></div>'

def render_cards(cs):
 body='<header><p class="eyebrow">Dusk & Dawn · working proposal</p><h1>Card effect catalogue</h1><p>496 individually reviewed faces. Every face costs 1 mana. The description is the whole effect: highlighted keywords explain a rule used in that description, and there are no separate theme tags.</p><p class="notice">Effects and values remain proposals. <a href="'+quote(GAME+'.html')+'#keywords">Keyword rules</a> · <a href="Full%20Content%20Review%20v0.1.html">Artwork review and changes</a></p><p class="muted">Binding and Release remain provisional damage labels; no replacement or opposing-theme taxonomy is assumed.</p></header>'+tools(248)
 pairs=collections.OrderedDict()
 for c in cs:pairs.setdefault(c['pair'],[]).append(c)
 for pair,faces in pairs.items():
  search=' '.join([pair]+[c['face']+' '+c['effect'] for c in faces]).lower()
  body+=f'<section class="pair" data-search="{html.escape(search,quote=True)}"><h2>{html.escape(pair)}</h2><div class="faces">'
  for c in faces:
   body+=f'<div><span class="side">{c["side"]} face</span><h3>{html.escape(c["face"])}</h3><p class="effect" data-face="{html.escape(c["face"],quote=True)}">{mark(c["effect"])}</p><a href="{html.escape(c["artwork_url"],quote=True)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View {html.escape(c["face"])} artwork</a></div>'
  body+='</div></section>'
 body+='<footer>All 496 artworks were inspected at contact-sheet scale. Thematic fit is a documented design judgment; balance and fun still need human playtests. Search indexes only names and actual effect text.</footer>'
 (DOCS/(CARD+'.html')).write_text(page('Dusk & Dawn — Card Effect Catalogue v0.2',body,filter_script('.pair',248)))

class ImageCache(HTMLParser):
 def __init__(self):super().__init__();self.id=None;self.images={}
 def handle_starttag(self,tag,attrs):
  a=dict(attrs)
  if tag=='article' and 'id' in a:self.id=a['id']
  if tag=='img' and self.id:self.images[self.id]=a['src']
 def handle_endtag(self,tag):
  if tag=='article':self.id=None

def render_enemies(es,rules):
 cache=ImageCache();cache.feed((DOCS/(ENEMY+'.html')).read_text());assert len(cache.images)==110
 body='<header><p class="eyebrow">Dusk & Dawn · 110 enemy proposals</p><h1>110 uncanny encounters</h1><p>Every enemy has an independently tuned action pool, one labeled trait and an explicit damage-type weakness. Values are not linked to player-card definitions.</p><p class="notice">'+mark(rules['Hush']['definition'])+'</p><p class="muted">Health and damage are first-test values, not playtested balance. Binding and Release remain provisional damage labels. <a href="'+quote(GAME+'.html')+'#encounters">Encounter rules</a> · <a href="Full%20Content%20Review%20v0.1.html">Individual artwork review</a></p></header>'+tools(110,options=[('reactive-trait','Reactive traits'),('temporary-card-loss','Temporary card loss'),('recovery-stall-check','Recovery / stall checks'),('visible-next-turn-effect','Next-turn effects')])+'<section class="grid" aria-label="Enemy catalogue">'
 lines=['DUSK & DAWN — ENEMY MECHANICS CATALOGUE v0.1','110 independently authored action pools · working proposal','All health and effect values require playtesting. No resistances. No separate theme tags.','Hush: '+rules['Hush']['definition'],'Leech: '+rules['Leech']['definition'],'']
 for e in es:
  acts={a['id']:a for a in e['actions']};rhythm=' → '.join(acts[k]['name'] for k in e['pattern'])
  search=' '.join([e['name'],e['trait']['name'],e['trait']['effect'],e['weakness']['type']]+[a['name']+' '+a['effect'] for a in e['actions']]).lower()
  body+=f'<article class="enemy" id="{e["id"]}" data-search="{html.escape(search,quote=True)}" data-filter="{html.escape(" ".join(e["review_flags"]),quote=True)}"><img class="art" src="{cache.images[e["id"]]}" alt="{html.escape(e["artwork"]["observed"],quote=True)}" width="320" height="240" loading="lazy"><div class="entry"><p class="number">{e["number"]:03} · {e["health"]} HP</p><h2>{html.escape(e["name"])}</h2><p><strong>Weakness:</strong> {mark(e["weakness"]["type"])} · +2 once per direct attack card.</p><p class="small">{html.escape(e["weakness"]["reason"])}</p><h3>Trait · {html.escape(e["trait"]["name"])}</h3><p>{mark(e["trait"]["effect"])}</p><h3>Action pool</h3><ul class="actions">'
  for a in e['actions']:
   body+=f'<li><strong>{html.escape(a["name"])}</strong><br>{mark(a["effect"])}'+(' <em>Uses the labeled trait.</em>' if a['trait_active'] else '')+'</li>'
  body+='</ul><p class="small rule"><strong>Pattern:</strong> '+html.escape(rhythm)+'. Repeat.</p><details><summary>Hush previews and review</summary>'
  for a in e['actions']:body+='<p><strong>'+html.escape(a['name'])+':</strong> '+mark(a['hushed_effect'])+'</p>'
  body+='<p><strong>Why it fits:</strong> '+html.escape(e['thematic_reason'])+'</p><p><strong>Weakness access:</strong> '+str(e['weakness']['available_direct_face_count'])+' direct faces in the current catalogue.</p><p><strong>Review flags:</strong> '+html.escape(', '.join(e['review_flags']) or 'No special gate; balance remains untested.')+'</p><p class="muted">Inspected: '+html.escape(e['artwork']['source_filename'])+'</p></details></div></article>'
  lines += [f'{e["number"]:03} {e["name"]} · {e["health"]} HP',f'  Weakness: {e["weakness"]["type"]}. {e["weakness"]["reason"]}',f'  Trait — {e["trait"]["name"]}: {e["trait"]["effect"]}']
  for a in e['actions']:lines += [f'  {a["name"]}: {a["effect"]}'+(' Uses the trait.' if a['trait_active'] else ''),f'    Hush: {a["hushed_effect"]}']
  lines += [f'  Pattern: {rhythm}. Repeat.',f'  Artwork fit: {e["thematic_reason"]}','']
 body+='</section><footer>All 110 source artworks were inspected. No Ward-versus-HP tests, prior-turn card comparisons or retained-card snapshots remain. Two reactive traits are explicitly labeled and visible while their intent is shown. The full action, including conditional and next-turn effects, must be previewed.</footer>'
 (DOCS/(ENEMY+'.html')).write_text(page(ENEMY,body,filter_script('.enemy',110)))
 (DOCS/(ENEMY+'.txt')).write_text('\n'.join(lines).rstrip()+'\n')

THOUGHTS=[
 ('Moth opening','The Radiant Moth has 18 HP and shows Folded-Wing Dust: 4 Radiance. Angel grants 5 Ward; Sun deals 6 Radiance. Its HP becomes 12; its hit uses 4 Ward and deals no HP damage. Open-Wing Dust is next: base 4 plus the trait’s 1.','Uses the canonical first encounter, not a separate Glass Judge fixture.'),
 ('Hush and extraction','The Dentist shows Pull: 4 Release, with Extraction removing 5 player Ward first. Against 5 Ward it deals 4 HP damage. Hush removes Extraction; all 4 damage is absorbed.','The base attack remains. No trait asks which layer took the hit.'),
 ('Hush and the choir','Chorus and Clutch has a base 2 Binding hit and two trait hits of 2. Hush leaves just the base 2. Weaken 3 without Hush instead produces hits of 0, 2 and 2.','With 3 Ward, the weakened action still deals 1 HP damage.'),
 ('Leech through Ward and overkill','A 4 Shadow Vampire attack against a Shadow weakness has final damage 6. It heals 6 even if Ward absorbs the hit or the enemy had only 1 HP. If the player was at 26/30 HP, healing stops at 30.','No HP-actually-lost counter is used.'),
 ('Leech after Weaken','Vampire’s base 4 plus 2 weakness is reduced by player Weaken 3. Final damage is 3, and Leech heals 3 before Ward changes the target’s HP.','Bonuses and Weaken precede Leech; Ward does not reduce it.'),
 ('A reflected hit','A 6-damage hit is reflected back once, with the same type and final value. It does not gain a new weakness or Mark bonus at the new target. If its attacker has 2 Ward, that Ward absorbs 2 and the attacker loses 4 HP.','A reflected hit cannot reflect again.'),
 ('A reactive mirror','While Mirror-Eyed Swan shows Raise the Mirror Wing, its first incoming direct hit is reflected. Hush played first suspends that reflection immediately; the Swan still performs its base 4 Radiance attack. Hush played after a reflected hit does not undo it.','Reactive traits act during the player turn and must be shown before a card is played.'),
 ('Thorns without a health gate','While Thorned Librarian shows Open the Brambles, each resolved direct attack card provokes 1 Binding trait damage if the Librarian survives. A hit fully absorbed by its Ward still provokes the thorn. Hush stops later pricks but does not refund an earlier one.','Reaction damage is not an attack and does not spend Reflect or Weaken.'),
 ('Burn feeds the mouth','Lantern Eater has 3 Burn at turn end. Burn deals 3 Flame and falls to 2. On Devour the Glow, the remaining Burn satisfies one condition for the whole trait: remove it and heal 3. With Hush, Burn stays at 2 and no feeding heal occurs.','The Burn condition is checked once for the action, not again after clearing Burn.'),
 ('A player Burn','The Kiln applies 2 Burn after the current turn’s Burn step. It first ticks at the end of the next player turn. A Rain played before then removes Burn from both combatants; Bathhouse removes only the player’s Burn.','Player Ward can absorb that tick before it expires at the next turn start.'),
 ('A visible tax','The Taxman’s Collect the Pearl applies a 1-mana refill reduction. The next player turn starts at 2 mana, not 3; the penalty then ends. Hush prevents its application but leaves the 4 Binding base hit.','No spent or unspent mana from the prior turn is inspected.'),
 ('The next hand’s face','Masked Midday’s trait schedules a light-facing hand. At the next normal draw, draw within the eight-card cap, then turn the entire held hand light-side up. Hush on the preceding enemy action prevents that schedule; Hush afterward cannot reverse an already completed turn.','The queued effect is visible; no card identity or retained snapshot is stored.'),
 ('Returning a changed form','Pottery Workshop chooses a card in the discard pile, flips that physical card there, then returns it to hand. Its source is resolving outside the hand and cannot be chosen.','Explicit zone text is the exception to ordinary hand-only Flip.'),
 ('Splitting a ray','Prism deals three hits of 2 Radiance. Against a Radiance weakness with Mark 3, the first hit is 7 and the next two are 2 each, before Ward. Weakness and Mark are not added to every ray.','One weakness bonus per played card; one Mark spend.'),
 ('A cost without a target','Oblivion requires another card in hand to Banish. If it is the only card, it cannot be played and spends no mana. A pure Scry with both piles empty simply does nothing.','Required costs differ from instructions that operate on whatever is available.'),
]

# Full game-design body is built below from the canonical card and enemy data.
def section(key,title,body):return f'<section id="{key}" class="section"><h2>{title}</h2>{body}</section>'
def p(s):return '<p>'+''.join(x if x.startswith('<a ') else mark(x) for x in re.split(r'(<a [^>]+>.*?</a>)',s))+'</p>'
def ul(items):return '<ul>'+''.join('<li>'+mark(x)+'</li>' for x in items)+'</ul>'
def build_game(cs,es):
 byface={x['face']:x for x in cs};byname={x['name']:x for x in es}
 body='<header><p class="eyebrow">Dusk & Dawn · design proposal · 3 November 2026</p><h1>A hand with two faces.<br>One uncanny enemy.</h1><p>Play a card’s visible effect or change the hand to find another answer. Build a small deck through a short run. Light and dark are moods and forms, never moral teams.</p><p class="notice">This is a design proposal, not a playable implementation or a claim of balanced values. All 496 card faces and 110 enemy artworks have a recorded individual thematic review.</p></header>'
 toc=[('idea','The idea'),('turn','A turn'),('rules','Core rules'),('keywords','Keywords'),('examples','Cards'),('encounters','Enemies'),('runs','A run'),('tests','Thought experiments'),('interface','Presentation'),('decisions','Open questions')]
 body+='<div class="portrait-grid" aria-label="Concept artwork"><img src="design-artwork/angel.jpg" alt="Angel cut-paper concept art"><img src="design-artwork/vampire.jpg" alt="Vampire cut-paper concept art"><img src="design-artwork/radiant-moth.jpg" alt="Radiant Moth cut-paper concept art"></div>'
 body+='<nav class="toc" aria-label="Contents">'+''.join(f'<a href="#{key}">{i:02} · {label}</a>' for i,(key,label) in enumerate(toc,1))+'</nav>'
 body+=section('idea','01 · The idea',p('Each physical card has a light face and a dark face. Spend 1 mana to play its visible effect. Some effects Flip held cards, revealing different options immediately. Face one enemy at a time, with its complete next action shown before deciding what to play.')+p('There is no battlefield, opposing deck, poker hand or score multiplier. Enemy actions use familiar rules with their own names and values. They do not secretly play player cards or share their balance definitions.'))
 body+=section('turn','02 · A turn',ul([
 'At the start of the player turn, expire player Ward, refill to 3 mana and draw up to 5 new cards within the 8-card hand cap. Apply any visible next-draw or refill modifier, then clear that modifier.',
 'Inspect the complete enemy intent: base hits, labeled trait, statuses, card movement and any conditional or next-turn effect. Play cards for 1 mana each.',
 'End the turn. Discard unkept cards; kept cards remain on their current faces and lose their markers.',
 'Resolve player Burn, then enemy Burn. Reduce each Burn by 1 after its hit. Defeat ends combat immediately, except that a player card already resolving finishes its effects if the enemy is defeated.',
 'If the enemy survives, expire its old Ward and resolve the displayed action. Hush suppresses its trait and skips a non-attack ability. Advance the pattern normally, end Hush, and reveal the next intent.'
 ]))
 body+=section('rules','03 · Core rules',
 '<h3>Cards, mana and targets</h3>'+ul([
 'Start a fight with the run deck shuffled, light-side up, at 3 maximum mana and with temporary effects cleared. Unspent mana does not carry over. Health carries between encounters.',
 'Every face costs 1 mana. Check mana and required choices before playing. Canceling a choice spends nothing. The source leaves the hand while resolving, so it cannot be “another card” and opens one hand slot.',
 'Resolve sentences in order. Required payments such as “Banish another card” must be available before play. An HP payment cannot reduce you to 0. A return from the discard pile also requires a destination slot.',
 'If an inspection or later instruction has fewer available cards than stated, use what is available. Optional “up to” choices may select zero; compulsory enemy moves use all available cards up to their stated number.',
 'The hand holds at most 8 cards. Excess draws stay in the draw pile. For each draw, reshuffle the discard pile when the draw pile is empty. If both are empty, stop.',
 'Before looking at or moving the top of an empty draw pile, reshuffle the discard pile. A multi-card inspection then uses the cards available in that draw pile; it does not reshuffle midway through inspection.',
 'Cards keep their faces through movement and reshuffling. Reset every card to its light face at the next encounter. No card copies are created, and banished cards cannot return during the fight.',
 'A mana-gain face grants at most 1 mana and must Banish itself. Mana never exceeds 3. Healing stops at maximum HP. These limits do not establish balance; test combinations.'
 ])+'<h3>Plain instructions</h3>'+ul([
 '“Turn your hand to its light faces” changes only dark faces; the dark-facing version changes only light faces. A chosen-card version requires a card that can turn. The resolving source is never in hand.',
 '“Look at the top 3 cards” names an inspection, not a new keyword. Put the chosen cards in the stated destination and order. If the hand has too few slots, choose only what fits; the rest use the stated remaining-card destination.',
 '“Exchange a card in your hand with one in your discard pile” requires both choices and swaps their zones, preserving their faces. A hand card cannot exchange with itself.',
 'Shuffling the hand into the draw pile preserves faces and clears Keep markers from cards that leave hand. Shuffle before drawing the stated replacement hand.',
 'A random choice uses only the stated current zone and shows the result. When the player moves several cards onto a pile, they choose the order unless the effect says otherwise. At turn end they may order their discarded cards.',
 'A queued draw or mana reduction affects the next normal draw or refill only, then ends. Use the larger pending reduction, not a sum; never go below 0. A queued face change happens after that next normal draw and affects the whole held hand. Show these pending effects.'
 ])+'<h3>Damage and defeat</h3>'+ul([
 'Every hit has exactly one printed damage type. Add Mark and any matching weakness bonus, then apply Weaken to the first hit, then Reflect if active, then Ward and HP. Show the final values before play.',
 'A matching weakness adds 2 to the first direct hit of a played card, once per card. Later hits keep their printed values. Utility effects, Burn, reflection and separate trait damage gain no weakness bonus.',
 'A card’s extra non-damage sentences still resolve when Ward absorbs its hit. No effect checks whether damage reached Ward or HP, or how much HP was actually lost. Leech uses the final damage value before Ward.',
 'Player HP at 0 ends the run immediately. A defeated enemy cannot start an action or provoke a new reaction. Finish the current player card’s remaining effects, including healing, then award victory. Leech cannot revive its defeated owner.',
 'Keep a clear concede control available. A player can remove too many damage cards through Banish; there is no hidden replacement or automatic rescue.'
 ]))
 kw='<p>The description is the whole effect. Highlight only keywords actually used there. There are no separate theme tags, hidden affinity effects, or extra tag chips. Plain instructions remain plain language; a face with no named keyword may use neutral presentation.</p><dl>'
 for name,d in RULES.items():kw+='<dt>'+mark(name)+'</dt><dd>'+mark(d['definition'])+ul(d['notes'])+'</dd>'
 kw+='</dl><h3>Typed damage and weaknesses</h3>'+p('Damage labels describe the hit, not an additional affinity. The current labels are '+', '.join(TYPES)+'. Each enemy names its own weakness; it is not inferred from a separate opposing-theme tag. Weakness matches the printed damage type, not a card’s name, artwork, side or an unprinted association.')+p('Binding and Release remain provisional names under review. No replacement pair is chosen here. Memory currently has no direct player attacks, so no enemy is assigned a Memory weakness. Wider-pool weaknesses must have matching direct attacks available in that pool.')
