 body+=section('encounters','06 · Enemy action pools',p('Each enemy has 2–3 named actions, one labeled trait and one explicit weakness. Perform one shown action per turn from a short repeating pattern. Preview the action before the player acts, including every hit, trait rider, status and card move. The values are independent of player cards, even when both use a familiar operation.')+p('Enemies have no hidden hand, deck, draw, Flip economy or mana pool. Their actions can explicitly affect the player’s real zones or statuses. Do not silently reinterpret a player-card effect or borrow its balance value by reference.')+p('Hush suspends reactive traits immediately, removes the upcoming trait contribution, and skips a non-attack ability. It does not remove the base hits or undo an earlier result. The Swan’s reflection and Librarian’s thorns are labeled as active while their intent is shown. Temporary counters and the computed intent are visible; no trait compares prior turns or remembered physical card IDs.')+p('This five-fight route is a first-test fixture. The table is generated from the revised roster, not maintained as a second conflicting set of enemies. Read the exact base effects and Hush previews in the <a href="'+quote(ENEMY+'.html')+'">110-enemy catalogue</a>.')+table+p('Banish, draw penalties, mana taxes, reactive reflection and forced next-hand faces belong in later curated encounters until players understand their previews. Card movements show their destination. Held-card effects use the current hand after discard and do nothing if it is empty. All affected player cards return after the fight if Banished.'))
