 body+=section('interface','09 · Presentation and interaction',p('Use the locked cut-paper theatre artwork. Player cards are full-bleed 3:4 portraits with no text, numbers or icons over the art. The enemy is a 4:3 landscape card with a minimal health bar in its frame. Keep intent, trait, HP, mana and status indicators beside the artwork.')+p('Hover or keyboard focus reveals the whole current effect and the relevant keyword explanations. Inspection works even when a card is unaffordable or has no valid target. On touch, inspect first and use a separate Play control. Show why a required choice is unavailable; canceling a choice spends nothing.')+p('A Flip preview shows exactly which held cards change and their resulting descriptions. A card drawn before Flip will turn too; do not reveal unknown draws. A card that leaves hand loses its Keep marker. Preview held-card hazards using the cards currently marked to remain, not a hidden historical snapshot.')+p('Enemy inspection separates base hits from the labeled trait, shows the complete repeating pattern, and offers the exact Hush result. Update conditional values during the player turn. Display queued draw, mana and facing changes. A pure Hush card may target a conditional trait before its condition is met, but not an intent with no suppressible effect or an enemy already Hushed.')+p('Use written keyword labels alongside color. Offer keyboard navigation, screen-reader descriptions, visible focus, reduced motion, optional reflections and persistent intent text. The current application remains a browsing foundation; these catalogues do not implement combat.'))
